**Test adequacy: the deleted-file filter is untested.**

Mutant: drop `&& Path::new(file).is_file()` from the `dirty` filter. A deleted tracked file still shows up in `git diff --name-only`, so the formatter and the lint would get a path that no longer exists, and every test in `tools/hooks-rs/tests/quality_checks.rs` would still pass.

Why no test catches it: the suite covers modified, untracked, staged and clean-tree cases. `no_dirty_source_file_runs_nothing` removes `wt/b.ts`, but that file is untracked, so git never lists it. The only committed source, `a.ts`, is never deleted.

A test along these lines would catch it (adjust it to the file's `Fixture` API):

```rust
#[test]
fn deleted_tracked_source_is_not_passed_to_the_tools() {
    let fixture = Fixture::new("deleted");
    std::fs::remove_file(fixture.wt.join("a.ts")).expect("delete the tracked file");
    let log = fixture.log_after(&stop(&fixture.wt));
    let want = format!("{} stub lint b.ts", fixture.wt.display());
    assert!(has_line(&log, &want), "want {want:?} in {log:?}");
}
```

